From 319851618baf259f59bcf5e8d434e495aae12ee1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niko Wu <wwh930329@163.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:02:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] provider, gateway: a usage-billed Claude seat keeps the
 overage window Claude Code tells (#4241)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An enterprise seat billed by usage has no 5-hour or 7-day window of its
own. Claude Code tells its one reading as rateLimitType "overage" in the
run's rate_limit_event, and calls the renewal overageResetsAt, apart from
resetsAt. claudeKinds had no "overage", so the reading was dropped: the
seat's card fell back to its /usage, which prints only the subscription
notice, and said no allowance was known.

- claudeKinds gains {"overage", "Extra usage", "", 0}: a span of its own of
  none, since it renews with the billing period.
- claudeLimits renews it at overageResetsAt when Claude Code names one,
  for the utilization and the rejected branches both.
- ratelimitWindows says it again as anthropic-ratelimit-unified-overage-*,
  the window a Claude Code signed in to claude.ai reads.

Tests: TestClaudeOverageSeatKeepsItsWindow (provider) — a seat whose /usage
prints the subscription notice keeps the heard 0.84 as "Extra usage";
TestNoteClaudeLimits now expects the fourth window; TestClaudeOverageSeatSaysItsWindow
(gateway) — the event's utilization and overageResetsAt reach the reply's
headers. Both are red on the tree before this change.

Ran: go test ./internal/provider/ ./internal/catalog/ — 1934 passed;
go test ./internal/gateway/ -timeout 45m — 428s, green but for four that are
red on upstream/main 4534561f on this machine (TestCodexFittedImagesPastTheBudget,
TestMarshalRawIsEncodingJSON, TestServeWSLListensBesideLoopback,
FuzzMarshalRaw/seed#7); gofmt -l and go vet clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
